.SH NAME
.PP
auto-xdm-toggle - Start or stop the XDM display manager

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-xdm-toggle state
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
state   "on" or "off"
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-xdm-toggle
command starts or stops the XDM display manager, which may be
running from /etc/ttys or as a service using an rc(8) script.

When disabling XDM using, any graphical login sessions will be
abuptly terminated and any unsaved data will be lost.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-xdm-toggle on
.ad
.fi

.SH FILES
.nf
.na
/etc/ttys
/etc/rc.conf
.ad
.fi

